.TH INDI_VIXEN_WIRELESSUNIT 1 "2026-09-24" "indi-vixen-wirelessunit 0.1.136" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
indi_vixen_wirelessunit \- INDI telescope driver for the Vixen Wireless Unit
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B indiserver
.RI [ options ]
.B indi_vixen_wirelessunit
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B indi_vixen_wirelessunit
is an INDI telescope and guider driver for the Vixen Wireless Unit.
It supports Vixen mounts such as the SXP2 and communicates with Wireless Unit
firmware 2.60 over UDP.
.PP
The driver provides device discovery, GoTo, synchronization, tracking,
parking, manual motion, pulse guiding, alignment management, mount settings,
and Wireless Unit Wi-Fi configuration.
.PP
The Main Control tab provides an optional Assume HOME setting. It is disabled
by default. When enabled, an uninitialized mount is initialized on Connect at
the current physical position, which must first be placed at azimuth 270
degrees and altitude 0 degrees. A failed attempt leaves manual Home set
available.
It is normally started by
.BR indiserver (1)
or by an INDI client such as KStars/Ekos, rather than run directly.
.SH NETWORK
The default Wireless Unit command port is UDP port 60023.
The Connection tab can discover a unit on local IPv4 networks or use a Host
and Port entered by the operator.
Automatic discovery attempts up to four searches at five-second intervals
when no unit responds. Disconnect cancels pending searches.
Manual Search performs one search.
An operator-edited endpoint is contacted directly without automatic discovery.
